# gitleaks allowlist. One fingerprint per line, in the form
# <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line> as printed by the Secret Scan job summary.
#
# Convention: every entry carries a comment above it stating who confirmed it is
# a false positive, on what date, and why the value is not a credential. An entry
# without a justification is not a valid entry and should be rejected in review.
#
# A fingerprint pins one rule to one line of one commit, so an entry cannot hide
# a different finding. Do not add path or regex allowlists to suppress noise in
# bulk. If a real secret is found, the answer is rotation, not an entry here.
# See docs/security/secret-scanning.md.
#
# Example:
#   # steven 2026-08-02: sample response body in a test fixture, the token field
#   # is a hand-written placeholder and authenticates to nothing.
#   1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b:src/__fixtures__/response.json:generic-api-key:12
